# Cloudflare Pages SPA routing.
#
# The app is a single-page React Router application: /courses, /gate,
# /live/<id> and the rest exist only in the browser, not as files on disk.
# Without this rule Pages looks for a matching file, finds none, and returns
# 404 for every route except "/" — including anyone who refreshes the page or
# opens a shared link.
#
# The 200 (rather than 301) serves index.html while keeping the URL, so the
# router sees the original path and renders the right screen.
#
# This replaces the equivalent redirect that lived in netlify.toml.
/*    /index.html   200
